{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> At the beginning." "<b>Like the gathering.</b> The reaper harvests the standing grain." "<b>And it shall be like one gleaning ears.</b> At the end, for the king of Assyria came against the land of Israel several times." "<b>In the valley of Rephaim.</b> It was a place whose harvest was poor, scant, and thin."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:05.585532997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}